{"ref":"BDB, מַעֲרָב³","hw":"מַעֲרָב³","html":"† I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">מַעֲרָב</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> usually <strong>coll. articles of exchange, merchandise</strong> (only of Tyre, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27\">Ez 27</a>);—sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַעֲרָבֵךְ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.17\">17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:25\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.25\">25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:27\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.27\">27</a> a.<a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:34\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.34\">34</a>; as acc. cogn. c. <span dir=\"rtl\">עָרַב</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:27\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.27\">27</a>; pl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַעֲרָבַיִךְ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.23\">33</a> perhaps <em>thy</em> (diverse) <em>wares</em> <strong>(</strong>DHM<sup>VOJ viii (1894), 4</sup> proposes, ingeniously, meaning <em>imports</em>, deriveing from. V. <span dir=\"rtl\">ערב</span> <em>enter</em>, but improb.<strong>)</strong>.","next":"BDB, תַּעֲרֻבָה","prev":"BDB, עֵרָבוֹן"}